1
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,670
A breakup story usually asks who hurt whom.

2
00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:17,390
This performance asks a more dangerous question:

3
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:19,930
who gets to define love after it fails?

4
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,350
In P4 Theater's 2021 p4U project,

5
00:00:57,630 --> 00:00:59,850
a disappointed lover enters a dreamlike world

6
00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:03,390
where private grief is immediately claimed by
competing systems.

7
00:01:03,550 --> 00:01:05,690
One voice calls love a perfect illusion

8
00:01:05,730 --> 00:01:08,010
and a chain on human freedom.

9
00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:10,230
Another treats romance as sacred,

10
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:12,710
arguing that love must be allowed every possible
form,

11
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:14,270
even when it produces pain.

12
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:44,750
Between them stands the middle:

13
00:01:45,150 --> 00:01:48,270
a person who wants both romantic intensity and
rational restraint,

14
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:50,510
yet cannot make those demands coexist.

15
00:01:50,770 --> 00:01:53,110
This position is not peaceful neutrality.

16
00:01:53,650 --> 00:01:56,170
It is a body being pulled by rival absolutes.

17
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:15,670
The performance gives those absolutes strange
physical forms.

18
00:02:15,710 --> 00:02:17,210
In a country without love,

19
00:02:17,590 --> 00:02:19,370
wooden lips promise to cure every sorrow.

20
00:02:19,950 --> 00:02:22,890
A budgerigar speaks as if it has escaped human
evolution.

21
00:02:23,490 --> 00:02:25,350
Temporary commitment is renamed absolute
freedom.

22
00:02:25,390 --> 00:02:26,990
Each doctrine offers liberation,

23
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:30,710
but only after asking the lover to surrender
language, memory, or judgment

24
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:32,750
to a supposedly greater order.

25
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:47,210
Then the argument becomes concrete.

26
00:02:47,770 --> 00:02:50,510
Fifteen minutes remain before the fifth
anniversary with Mino.

27
00:02:50,690 --> 00:02:54,710
The same fifteen minutes also lead toward a
Saturday date with another woman.

28
00:02:54,850 --> 00:02:56,470
Time itself becomes a tribunal.

29
00:02:56,790 --> 00:02:58,550
The character can postpone the decision,

30
00:02:58,790 --> 00:03:01,110
but postponement is already shaping the lives
around him.

31
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,090
This is larger than relationship advice.

32
00:03:51,510 --> 00:03:54,330
The work treats love as an ideological
battlefield.

33
00:03:55,470 --> 00:03:57,450
Anti-romance can become as dogmatic as romance.

34
00:03:57,730 --> 00:03:59,310
Freedom can conceal obedience.

35
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:01,430
Accept every form of love sounds generous,

36
00:04:01,470 --> 00:04:05,890
until someone asks whether every form should
also be allowed to ignore social order.

37
00:04:06,730 --> 00:04:10,290
The original project invited its audience to
affect the dramatic outcome.

38
00:04:10,490 --> 00:04:13,210
To choose was to expose the assumptions behind
the choice.

39
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:34,870
Self-rescue may not mean finding the correct
camp.

40
00:04:34,910 --> 00:04:39,110
It may begin by noticing how every camp recruits
our disappointment,

41
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:42,430
gives it a name, and tells us what to do next.

42
00:04:42,870 --> 00:04:44,450
The middle can be cowardice.

43
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:47,470
It can also be the last place where
contradiction remains visible

44
00:04:47,510 --> 00:04:49,810
before a slogan closes it down.

45
00:04:50,130 --> 00:04:52,810
When every theory of love demands total loyalty,

46
00:04:52,850 --> 00:04:55,570
is refusing to choose an escape from
responsibility—

47
00:04:55,610 --> 00:04:57,070
or the beginning of freedom?
